        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p64-q29-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "C'(x)=\\begin{cases}1&1<x<2,\\\\2&2<x<4,\\\\\\frac13&4<x<7.\\end{cases}",
                    "display": true
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p64-q29-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use each segment's slope; mark the segment endpoints with open circles.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Let $C(x)$ denote the cumulative frequency. The derivative on each straight segment is its slope.\n$$\\begin{align*}C'(x)&=\\frac{1-0}{2-1}=1 &&(1<x<2),\\\\C'(x)&=\\frac{5-1}{4-2}=2 &&(2<x<4),\\\\C'(x)&=\\frac{6-5}{7-4}=\\frac13 &&(4<x<7).\\end{align*}$$\nSketch these three horizontal segments with open endpoints. The derivative is undefined at the corners $x=2,4$; the outer endpoints are also left open.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p64-q29-a-solution-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"derivativeBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"Derivative graph series\"}],\"reference\":\"PDF64 p64-q29-a; teacher PDF81 printed659\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.65cm,y=1.45cm,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{derivativeBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-0.5,-0.45) rectangle (8.6,2.65);\n\\draw[black,->,line width=0.5pt] (0.5,0)--(8.4,0);\n\\draw[black,->,line width=0.5pt] (0.5,0)--(0.5,2.5);\n\\foreach \\x in {1,2,4,7}{\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (\\x,0)--(\\x,0.06);\\node[below] at (\\x,0) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\x$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\foreach \\y/\\lab in {0.5/0.5,1/1.0,1.5/1.5,2/2.0}{\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (0.5,\\y)--(0.62,\\y);\\node[left] at (0.5,\\y) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\lab$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\draw[derivativeBlue,line width=0.8pt] (1,1)--(2,1);\n\\draw[derivativeBlue,line width=0.8pt] (2,2)--(4,2);\n\\draw[derivativeBlue,line width=0.8pt] (4,{1/3})--(7,{1/3});\n\\foreach \\x/\\y in {1/1,2/1,2/2,4/2,4/0.3333333333,7/0.3333333333}{\\draw[black,fill=white,line width=0.4pt] (\\x,\\y) circle[radius=1.3pt];}\n\\node[below] at (8.2,0) {$X$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 72,
